.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt USERDEL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm userdel
.Nd delete a user account
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl f
.Ar USER
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
removes
.Ar USER
from
.Pa /etc/passwd
and
.Pa /etc/shadow ,
strips the user from every supplementary-member list in
.Pa /etc/group
(and
.Pa /etc/gshadow ,
when present), and \(em if the per-user group has no other members and
the user's name matches the group's name \(em removes that primary
group as well, matching the
.Dv USERGROUPS_ENAB
convention.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl r
Also remove the user's home directory (recursively) and mail spool
.Pa ( /var/spool/mail/USER ) .
.It Fl f
Force deletion even if the user is "in use" \(em accepted for parity
with shadow-utils; the live-process scan is not yet implemented in
substrate's
.Nm .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 2
Bad usage.
.It 6
.Ar USER
does not exist.
.It 10
Failed to update
.Pa /etc/passwd .
.It 12
.Fl r
specified but the home directory could not be removed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr shadow 5 ,
.Xr useradd 8 ,
.Xr usermod 8 ,
.Xr groupdel 8
.Sh AUTHORS
Substrate-native
.Nm ,
written to match the shadow-utils command-line surface.
